<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">RISC-V Summit&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;talk proposal&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;structure draft for review</p>
    <h1>Optimize 1-bit LLM for<br>RISC-V Edge Devices</h1>
    <p class="thesis">
      A 27-billion-parameter model, one bit per weight, running on <b>a single in-order RISC-V
      core</b>. We took the stock llama.cpp kernel from 25% vector utilization to
      <b>11.9x faster decode</b> using three portable RVV changes and one stock Andes vendor
      instruction, and we measured every step on <b>pre-silicon RTL</b>.
    </p>

    <div class="proof">
      <div class="pf">
        <div class="n">27B</div>
        <div class="l">largest of three models</div>
        <div class="d">27B, 8B and 4B all produce correct text on one AX46MPV hart</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pf">
        <div class="n">11.9x</div>
        <div class="l">decode speedup</div>
        <div class="d">vs upstream llama.cpp, same numerics, cycle-accurate</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pf">
        <div class="n">3 modes</div>
        <div class="l">andesim, one simulator</div>
        <div class="d">functional, per-kernel exact, and full cycle-accurate from reset</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reviewnote">
      <div class="t">This is the skeleton, not the talk</div>
      <p>
        Every section below shows its <b>job</b>, the <b>claim</b> it makes, and the
